it's your most precious part?

517
00:38:18.560 --> 00:38:21.160
- ( whistles )
- Please.

518
00:38:21.320 --> 00:38:24.080
( sobbing )
No.

519
00:38:24.240 --> 00:38:26.120
No! Mercy. please!

520
00:38:26.280 --> 00:38:27.960
Please. mercy! Mercy!

521
00:38:28.120 --> 00:38:31.240
This is mercy.

522
00:38:31.400 --> 00:38:33.360
I'm not killing you.

523
00:38:33.520 --> 00:38:36.560
Just making a few alterations.

524
00:38:39.080 --> 00:38:41.080
No! No! No!

525
00:38:41.240 --> 00:38:42.960
Please. no! No!

526
00:38:43.120 --> 00:38:46.000
No! No. please!
Please!

527
00:38:48.880 --> 00:38:50.240
You're gonna scare it off.

528
00:38:50.400 --> 00:38:54.600
I'm not gonna scare it.
I'm gonna kill it.

529
00:38:54.760 --> 00:38:56.120
It's too far away.

530
00:39:18.680 --> 00:39:20.200
Is that a palace?

531
00:39:23.280 --> 00:39:25.520
It's a windmill.

532
00:39:25.680 --> 00:39:28.160
Windmill.

533
00:39:28.320 --> 00:39:31.240
Who built it? Some king?

534
00:39:31.400 --> 00:39:33.200
Just the men who used to live here.

535
00:39:33.360 --> 00:39:36.640
Ygritte: They must have been great
builders. stacking stones so high.

536
00:39:36.800 --> 00:39:39.720
Winterfell has towers
three times that size.

537
00:39:39.880 --> 00:39:42.480
( mocking ) "I'm Jon Snow
and I'm from Winterfell.

538
00:39:42.640 --> 00:39:46.800
My daddy was a fancy lord and I lived
in a tower that touched the clouds."

539
00:39:46.960 --> 00:39:48.320
If you're impressed by a windmill.

540
00:39:48.480 --> 00:39:51.520
you'd be swooning if you saw
the Great Keep at Winterfell.

541
00:39:51.680 --> 00:39:53.080
What's swooning?

542
00:39:53.240 --> 00:39:55.600
Fainting.

543
00:39:55.760 --> 00:39:57.800
What's fainting?

544
00:40:00.200 --> 00:40:01.960
When a girl sees blood and collapses.

545
00:40:02.120 --> 00:40:03.920
Why would a girl see blood
and collapse?

546
00:40:04.080 --> 00:40:06.880
Well...

547
00:40:07.040 --> 00:40:10.040
Not all girls are like you.

548
00:40:10.200 --> 00:40:13.040
Well. girls see more blood than boys.

549
00:40:13.200 --> 00:40:15.960
Or do you like girls who swoon.
Jon Snow?

550
00:40:16.120 --> 00:40:17.680
( gasps )
Oh. a spider!

551
00:40:17.840 --> 00:40:20.160
Save me. Jon Snow.

552
00:40:20.320 --> 00:40:24.960
My dress is made of the purest silk
from Tralalalaleeday.

553
00:40:25.120 --> 00:40:27.040
I'd like to see you in a silk dress.

554
00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:31.480
Would you?

555
00:40:34.160 --> 00:40:36.760
So I could tear it off you.

556
00:40:36.920 --> 00:40:42.080
Well. you rip my pretty silk dress.
I'll blacken your eye.

557
00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:52.000
Maybe one day
I'll take you to Winterfell.

558
00:40:52.160 --> 00:40:54.680
Or maybe one day
I'll take you there.

559
00:40:54.840 --> 00:40:56.640
After we've taken our land back.

560
00:40:59.920 --> 00:41:01.240
Ygritte.

561
00:41:04.560 --> 00:41:06.280
You won't win.

562
00:41:08.160 --> 00:41:09.800
I know your people are brave.
no one denies that.

563
00:41:09.960 --> 00:41:11.280
You know nothing...

564
00:41:11.440 --> 00:41:13.080
Six times in the last thousand years.

565
00:41:13.240 --> 00:41:15.680
a King-beyond-the-Wall
has attacked the kingdoms.

566
00:41:15.840 --> 00:41:18.760
- Six times they failed.
- And how do you know that?

567
00:41:18.920 --> 00:41:20.760
Every boy in the North knows it.

568
00:41:20.920 --> 00:41:23.360
We grow up learning it.
Where the battles were fought.

569
00:41:23.520 --> 00:41:25.040
the names of the heroes.
who died where.

570
00:41:25.200 --> 00:41:30.640
Six times you've invaded
and six times you've failed.

571
00:41:30.800 --> 00:41:32.160
The seventh will be the same.

572
00:41:32.320 --> 00:41:35.240
- Mance is different.
- You don't have the discipline.

573
00:41:35.400 --> 00:41:38.600
You don't have the training.
Your army is no army.

574
00:41:38.760 --> 00:41:40.080
You don't know how to fight together.

575
00:41:40.240 --> 00:41:42.960
- You don't know that.
- I do.

576
00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:44.440
I know it.

577
00:41:44.600 --> 00:41:46.600
If you attack the Wall. you'll die.

578
00:41:46.760 --> 00:41:49.320
All of you.

579
00:41:56.560 --> 00:41:58.000
All of us.

580
00:42:13.600 --> 00:42:18.120
You're mine as I'm yours.

581
00:42:18.280 --> 00:42:21.360
And if we die. we die.

582
00:42:21.520 --> 00:42:23.720
But first we'll live.

583
00:42:23.880 --> 00:42:27.360
Yes. first we'll live.

584
00:42:38.920 --> 00:42:43.240
( Jojen speaking quietly )

585
00:42:43.400 --> 00:42:45.880
What's he going on about?

586
00:42:46.040 --> 00:42:48.240
And how come
he always gets to sit and chat

587
00:42:48.400 --> 00:42:50.280
while we do all the work?

588
00:42:53.160 --> 00:42:55.280
Hodor.

589
00:42:56.560 --> 00:42:59.440
- That's where we are.
- What are you telling him?

590
00:42:59.600 --> 00:43:01.680
- It's all right. Osha.
- It's not all right.

591
00:43:01.840 --> 00:43:04.960
You think I can't hear you every day?
Filling his head with black magic.

592
00:43:05.120 --> 00:43:07.160
Talking about visions
and three-eyed ravens and worse.

593
00:43:07.320 --> 00:43:10.840
- Leave him alone.
- He can speak for himself.

594
00:43:11.000 --> 00:43:12.320
I don't fill his head with anything.

595
00:43:12.480 --> 00:43:14.720
Osha:
So what do you talk about?

596
00:43:14.880 --> 00:43:17.520
What's happening to him
and what that means.

597
00:43:17.680 --> 00:43:20.120
Go on. then.
Tell us what it means.

598
00:43:20.280 --> 00:43:23.160
It's not like that. I wish
I could tell him all the answers.

599
00:43:23.320 --> 00:43:26.040
It would be much easier.

600
00:43:26.200 --> 00:43:28.160
I don't want you
talking to him anymore.

601
00:43:28.320 --> 00:43:29.800
Until we get to your brother
at Castle Black.

602
00:43:29.960 --> 00:43:32.600
- We're not going to Castle Black.
- What did you say?

603
00:43:32.760 --> 00:43:36.240
I told you already.
Jon Snow isn't there.

604
00:43:36.400 --> 00:43:38.080
Bran needs to find the raven
beyond the Wall.

605
00:43:38.240 --> 00:43:40.920
Oh. no. I'm not going back there.
Your brother is at Castle Black.

606
00:43:41.080 --> 00:43:44.080
That's where we're going.

607
00:43:44.240 --> 00:43:47.240
Look at me.

608
00:43:47.400 --> 00:43:51.120
The raven's been coming to me
ever since I fell from that tower.

609
00:43:51.280 --> 00:43:53.800
He wants me to find him.

610
00:43:53.960 --> 00:43:58.880
I don't have my legs anymore.
This is what I have now.

611
00:43:59.040 --> 00:44:01.160
You have a family.

612
00:44:01.320 --> 00:44:02.800
You need to go back to Castle Black

613
00:44:02.960 --> 00:44:06.000
so you can get back to them
where you belong.

614
00:44:06.160 --> 00:44:08.320
What if I belong in the North?

615
00:44:08.480 --> 00:44:13.160
What if I fell from that tower
for a reason?

616
00:44:13.320 --> 00:44:16.880
Is that what he's telling you?
That it's all for a reason?

617
00:44:17.040 --> 00:44:18.360
All these bad things happened

618
00:44:18.520 --> 00:44:21.520
because the gods got big plans
for you?

619
00:44:21.680 --> 00:44:23.480
I wish it were true. little lord.
but the gods wouldn't spare

620
00:44:23.640 --> 00:44:26.840
a raven's cold shit
for you or me or anyone.

621
00:44:27.000 --> 00:44:29.080
You don't understand.
You don't know.

622
00:44:29.240 --> 00:44:30.960
You don't know.
None of you know.

623
00:44:31.120 --> 00:44:34.000
None of you have been up there.

624
00:44:36.320 --> 00:44:41.720
I had a man once.
A good man. Bruni. his name was.

625
00:44:41.880 --> 00:44:44.800
I was his and he was mine.

626
00:44:44.960 --> 00:44:48.160
But one night Bruni disappears.

627
00:44:48.320 --> 00:44:51.480
People said he left me.
but I knew him.

628
00:44:51.640 --> 00:44:55.080
He'd never leave me.
Not for long.

629
00:44:56.120 --> 00:44:59.240
I knew he'd come back.

630
00:44:59.400 --> 00:45:00.920
And he did.

631
00:45:02.400 --> 00:45:05.160
He came in
through the back of the hut.

632
00:45:06.440 --> 00:45:10.440
Only it wasn't Bruni. Not really.

633
00:45:11.440 --> 00:45:17.360
His skin was pale
like a dead man's.

634
00:45:17.520 --> 00:45:19.800
His eyes bluer than clear sky.

635
00:45:23.640 --> 00:45:27.120
He came at me.
grabbed me by the neck

636
00:45:27.280 --> 00:45:30.040
and squeezed so hard

637
00:45:30.200 --> 00:45:32.480
I could feel the life
slipping out of me.

638
00:45:35.360 --> 00:45:37.360
I don't know how I got the knife.

639
00:45:37.520 --> 00:45:43.200
When I did.
I stuck it deep into his heart.

640
00:45:45.960 --> 00:45:49.840
And he hardly seemed to notice.

641
00:45:50.000 --> 00:45:54.240
I had to burn our hut down
with him inside.

642
00:45:56.200 --> 00:45:58.720
I didn't ask the gods what it meant.

643
00:45:58.880 --> 00:46:02.480
I didn't need to. I already knew.

644
00:46:02.640 --> 00:46:05.560
It meant the North was no place
for men to be.

645
00:46:05.720 --> 00:46:07.480
Not anymore.

646
00:46:09.880 --> 00:46:12.000
I promised your maester
I'd get you to Castle Black

647
00:46:12.160 --> 00:46:14.360
and no further.

648
00:46:22.680 --> 00:46:24.080
Qyburn:
How is the pain. my lord?

649
00:46:27.160 --> 00:46:29.960
What's the purpose of an arm
with no hand?

650
00:46:33.920 --> 00:46:36.520
Well. we've stymied
the corruption.

651
00:46:36.680 --> 00:46:39.200
Yes. we've stymied
the corruption.

652
00:46:39.360 --> 00:46:41.160
You're a learned man.

653
00:46:41.320 --> 00:46:42.640
All the good it's done me.

654
00:46:42.800 --> 00:46:45.520
You did well sewing up this mess.

655
00:46:45.680 --> 00:46:47.120
You're far better
at this sort of work

656
00:46:47.280 --> 00:46:50.000
than Grand Maester Pycelle.

657
00:46:50.160 --> 00:46:52.760
Faint praise. my lord.

658
00:46:54.040 --> 00:46:56.880
So why did the Citadel take
your chain?

659
00:46:57.040 --> 00:46:58.840
Did you fondle one boy too many?

660
00:46:59.000 --> 00:47:01.720
No. my lord.
That's not my weakness.

661
00:47:03.520 --> 00:47:05.360
What is?

662
00:47:07.760 --> 00:47:09.240
Curiosity.

663
00:47:09.400 --> 00:47:13.280
The only way to treat disease
is to understand disease.

664
00:47:13.440 --> 00:47:17.920
And the only way to understand it
is to study the afflicted.

665
00:47:18.080 --> 00:47:19.920
You performed experiments
on living men.

666
00:47:20.080 --> 00:47:21.840
- On dying men.
- With their permission?

667
00:47:22.000 --> 00:47:26.360
My studies have given me insight
that has saved many lives.

668
00:47:26.520 --> 00:47:28.920
Dying paupers. I assume.

669
00:47:29.080 --> 00:47:32.480
Men with no families to complain.

670
00:47:32.640 --> 00:47:34.040
You found them moaning
in the poorhouse

671
00:47:34.200 --> 00:47:36.760
and had them carted back
to your garret

672
00:47:36.920 --> 00:47:39.680
and opened up their bellies
to see what was inside.

673
00:47:39.840 --> 00:47:42.960
How many men have you killed.
my lord?

674
00:47:43.120 --> 00:47:47.640
- I don't know.
- 50? 100?

675
00:47:48.640 --> 00:47:50.520
Countless.

676
00:47:50.680 --> 00:47:52.280
Countless has a nice ring to it.

677
00:47:52.440 --> 00:47:54.680
And how many lives have you saved?

678
00:47:54.840 --> 00:47:57.040
Half a million.

679
00:47:58.520 --> 00:48:00.320
The population of King's Landing.

680
00:48:05.680 --> 00:48:08.840
You were in charge of the ravens
at Harrenhal.

681
00:48:09.000 --> 00:48:13.080
Did you... Did you get a bird
off to Brienne's father in Tarth?

682
00:48:13.240 --> 00:48:16.600
A bird flew off and a bird flew back.

683
00:48:16.760 --> 00:48:20.800
Lord Selwyn Tarth offered
300 gold dragons

684
00:48:20.960 --> 00:48:22.800
for his daughter's safe return.

685
00:48:22.960 --> 00:48:25.920
- A fair offer.
- A fair offer. Locke won't take it.

686
00:48:28.200 --> 00:48:29.520
Why not?

687
00:48:29.680 --> 00:48:33.320
He's convinced Lord Tarth owns
all the sapphire mines in Westeros.

688
00:48:33.480 --> 00:48:34.880
( sighs )

689
00:48:35.040 --> 00:48:37.480
He feels he's being cheated.

690
00:48:37.640 --> 00:48:39.360
They'd be fools to kill her.

691
00:48:39.520 --> 00:48:41.520
These men have been at war
a long time.

692
00:48:41.680 --> 00:48:43.760
Most of them will be dead by winter.

693
00:48:43.920 --> 00:48:47.480
She'll be
their entertainment tonight.

694
00:48:47.640 --> 00:48:51.520
Beyond tonight. I don't think
they care very much.

695
00:49:09.480 --> 00:49:12.200
We have to return to Harrenhal.

696
00:49:12.360 --> 00:49:14.240
- Why?
- I've left something behind.

697
00:49:14.400 --> 00:49:17.840
Absolutely not.
I've got orders from Lord Bolton.

698
00:49:18.000 --> 00:49:19.480
And what are those orders?

699
00:49:19.640 --> 00:49:23.320
To deliver you to your father
at King's Landing.

700
00:49:23.480 --> 00:49:26.960
You think you'll get a reward.

701
00:49:27.120 --> 00:49:31.040
I serve Lord Bolton.
Any appreciation your father...

702
00:49:31.200 --> 00:49:33.760
You think you're getting a reward.
Let me explain something to you.

703
00:49:33.920 --> 00:49:36.280
When my father sees me.
the first thing he's going to ask

704
00:49:36.440 --> 00:49:38.000
is what happened to my hand.
And I'm going to tell him

705
00:49:38.160 --> 00:49:41.120
- ...this man chopped it off.
- I had nothing...

706
00:49:41.280 --> 00:49:46.720
Or I could tell him
this man saved my life.

707
00:49:46.880 --> 00:49:48.720
We return to Harrenhal now.

708
00:50:04.280 --> 00:50:07.600
( birds cawing )

709
00:50:07.760 --> 00:50:09.400
Whoa.

710
00:50:11.320 --> 00:50:13.080
- Eyes open. lads.
- Be quiet.

711
00:50:13.240 --> 00:50:16.720
( distant men singing )

712
00:50:18.080 --> 00:50:21.120
Men: <i>The bear. the bear</i>
<i>and the maiden fair</i>

713
00:50:21.280 --> 00:50:23.400
<i>From there to here.</i>
<i>from here to there</i>

714
00:50:23.560 --> 00:50:25.680
<i>All black and brown</i>
<i>and covered in hair</i>

715
00:50:25.840 --> 00:50:27.760
<i>He smelled that girl</i>
<i>in the summer air</i>

716
00:50:27.920 --> 00:50:30.000
<i>The bear. the bear.</i>
<i>and the maiden fair!</i>

717
00:50:30.160 --> 00:50:31.560
( cheering )

718
00:50:34.400 --> 00:50:36.160
Man:
Don't spare her.

719
00:50:36.320 --> 00:50:37.760
Don't spare her!

720
00:50:37.920 --> 00:50:40.240
( roaring )

721
00:50:40.400 --> 00:50:43.560
Well. this is one shameful
fucking performance.

722
00:50:43.720 --> 00:50:45.240
Stop running and fight.

723
00:50:45.400 --> 00:50:46.960
( bear growling )

724
00:50:52.320 --> 00:50:53.920
A wooden sword?

725
00:50:54.080 --> 00:50:56.720
- I thought you'd gone.
- You gave her a wooden sword.

726
00:50:56.880 --> 00:50:59.600
- We've only got one bear.
- I'll pay her bloody ransom.

727
00:50:59.760 --> 00:51:03.480
Gold. sapphires. whatever you want.
Just get her out of there.

728
00:51:03.640 --> 00:51:06.360
All you lords and ladies still think

729
00:51:06.520 --> 00:51:08.560
that the only thing that matters
is gold.

730
00:51:08.720 --> 00:51:12.480
This makes me happier
than all your gold ever could.

731
00:51:12.640 --> 00:51:14.840
And that makes me happier
than all her sapphires.

732
00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:19.600
So go buy yourself a golden hand
and fuck yourself with it.

733
00:51:22.320 --> 00:51:23.800
( roaring )

734
00:51:29.000 --> 00:51:30.880
Ah!

735
00:51:38.000 --> 00:51:39.320
- Get behind me.
- I will not.

736
00:51:39.480 --> 00:51:42.080
( groans )

737
00:51:48.400 --> 00:51:49.840
( growls )

738
00:51:50.000 --> 00:51:52.040
What the fuck are you doing
to my bear?

739
00:51:52.200 --> 00:51:54.000
Lord Bolton charged me
with bringing him back

740
00:51:54.160 --> 00:51:56.800
to King's Landing alive
and that's what I aim to do.

741
00:52:00.560 --> 00:52:02.720
Pull her up.

742
00:52:15.040 --> 00:52:17.280
Hold my legs.

743
00:52:24.160 --> 00:52:26.280
( roaring )

744
00:52:38.560 --> 00:52:39.960
Pull him up!

745
00:52:44.280 --> 00:52:46.240
( men booing )

746
00:52:50.080 --> 00:52:51.880
The bitch stays.

747
00:52:54.640 --> 00:52:57.800
We're taking her to King's Landing.
Unless you kill me.

748
00:53:00.640 --> 00:53:04.760
She belongs to me.
Lord Bolton's orders.

749
00:53:04.920 --> 00:53:07.480
What do you think is more important
to Lord Bolton?

750
00:53:07.640 --> 00:53:09.040
Getting his pet rat a reward

751
00:53:09.200 --> 00:53:13.880
or ensuring Tywin Lannister
gets his son back alive?

752
00:53:25.120 --> 00:53:28.480
( bear roaring )

753
00:53:32.240 --> 00:53:34.600
Well. we must be on our way.

754
00:53:38.400 --> 00:53:40.240
Sorry about the sapphires.

755
00:53:56.160 --> 00:54:00.160
( bear roaring )

756
00:54:00.320 --> 00:54:03.280
( music playing )
